# Append-only records that TWO crons write. The Monday grading run and the
# Tuesday send run each commit and push their own copy, so a push race is
# routine — and `git pull --rebase` on a normal text file turns that race into a
# conflict, which fails the persist step and LOSES published probabilities that
# cannot be recorded retroactively (a call is recorded at the moment it is
# published or not at all).
#
# `union` concatenates both sides instead of conflicting. It can duplicate the
# overlapping lines, which is why engine/ledger.py collapses by call_id on read
# and refuses — loudly — when two rows for one call disagree on the outcome.
data/processed/ledger/**/*.jsonl merge=union
data/processed/sent.jsonl        merge=union
